-- MAGIC %md
-- MAGIC ## A. Metastore Layout

-- COMMAND ----------

-- MAGIC %md-sandbox
-- MAGIC ### A1. Single Metastore per Region
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC Databricks recommends one metastore per region primarily to provide a unified governance architecture and prevent data silos, while ensuring performance, consistency, and regional isolation. Having a single metastore per region makes it simpler to manage permissions, audit logs, and organize data across multiple workspaces in that region. This pattern helps avoid confusion and metadata inconsistency, which can occur when the same data is registered in multiple metastores.
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC Here is a breakdown of why Databricks recommends a single metastore per cloud region:
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC - **Unified Namespace and Governance:** a single metastore enables a common namespace and centralizes governance, so organizations can share data securely and consistently across different teams and business units in the same region. 
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC - **Performance and Latency:** Unity Catalog is designed to provide low-latency access to metadata at the regional level. Assigning a metastore to a region ensures that metadata queries remain performant. 
-- MAGIC - **Regional Isolation and Compliance:** Data governance, access control, and audit logging are enforced at the metastore level, guaranteeing that regional compliance and security policies can be maintained without accidental cross-region access. 
-- MAGIC - **Consistency and Simplified Operations:** Registering tables in multiple metastores can lead to schema drift, property mismatches, and confusion over the true state of your data. Databricks strongly advises against this practice and instead recommends using OpenSharing to share data across regions when needed.
-- MAGIC
