-- COMMAND ----------

-- MAGIC %md-sandbox
-- MAGIC ### A2. Multiple Metastores per Region
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC While the default best practice is to use one metastore per region, some organizations may need multiple metastores in the same region. This is rare, and exceptions are granted only after careful review and approval from Databricks Product Management:
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC - **Organizational or Legal Segregation:** very large enterprises with completely independent legal entities or business units in the same region may need separate metastores to guarantee autonomy and strong segregation. 
-- MAGIC - **Strict Prod/Non-Prod Separation:** sometimes, compliance or operational mandates forbid any metadata or governance overlap between production and non-production environments, even within a single region.
-- MAGIC - **Disaster Recovery Requirements:** Some customers may implement additional metastores for DR purposes, especially when regional failover strategies are involved. 
-- MAGIC - **Subsidiaries and Mergers:** organizations operating multiple subsidiaries under one account, each with wholly separate operations and governance requirements, might require more than one metastore per region. 
-- MAGIC - **Quota or Capacity Constraints:** exceptionally large data estates (hundreds of thousands of tables, for example) may hit system soft limits, requiring additional metastores. 
