-- COMMAND ----------

-- MAGIC %md-sandbox
-- MAGIC #### C2.2 Hierarchical Assignment of Managed Storage
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC UC allows organizations to define managed storage locations at the metastore, catalog, or schema level. This means, for example, data in one catalog can be forced to reside in a dedicated bucket or container, while different teams or environments can have their own catalogs with separated storage. 
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC Using catalogs as the primary unit of governance, organizations can segregate data by business unit, team, or environment and bind those catalogs to specific workspaces for additional isolation. This ensures only the intended users have access to the data in that catalog. 
-- MAGIC <div style="display:flex; justify-content:center;">
